<p>  Durables		170.84  170.80   168.47  168.50   167.77</p>
<p> ORDERS-PCT CHANGES:    Sept--(Prev)	Aug--(Prev)    July</p>
<p>  Primary Metals	  -1.3   -1.7	-3.9   -4.0	1.6</p>
<p>  Industrial Machinery  -0.5   -0.9	-0.7   -0.8	2.8</p>
<p>  Electrical Equipment  -0.5    1.9	-5.3   -5.2	4.9</p>
<p>  Transport Equipment   19.8   17.5	-8.8   -8.8     -1.5</p>
<p> ORDERS-BLNS OF DLRS:   Sept--(Prev)	Aug--(Prev)     July</p>
<p>  Primary Metals	 14.98   14.91    15.18   15.16    15.80</p>
<p>  Industrial Machin.   32.19   32.05    32.35   32.34    32.59</p>
<p>  Electrical Equip.    26.47   27.14    26.60   26.62    28.07</p>
<p>  Transport Equip.     44.93   44.07    37.50   37.51    41.13</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected a 2.3 percent rise in total factory orders for September.</p>
<p>The department said the 2.7 percent increase in September factory orders was the biggest monthly increase since an identical gain in August 1994.  </p>
<p>Commerce said the 19.8 percent increase in September transportation was the first monthly rise since May and the biggest increase since December 1990 when it rose 20.2 percent.</p>
<p>The September inventories-to-shipments ratio was unchanged from 1.39 in August.</p>
<p>The department reported initial data on September orders for durable goods on October 25.</p>
